sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at the Aurelia aurita 201 µm ocellus scale — MorphoEval overall 85.0/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the Holocene 201 µm Schnakenberg node (chronoseries 1/1, age 0 Ma). Dispersion Pearson r = 0.9999, RMSE = 0.017, KS = 0.167. Patch FFT wavelength is 0.0002027 m against the assigned 0.0002006 m. The equal-diffusion field (std 3e-5, sigma_max = -0.102) is drawn on the patterned colour scale and is blank. Bell-body circularity is 0.462 against 1. The oral-bell lobe counter returned 1 against four gonads; that miss is reported and not repaired by editing the reference. Computer-vision similarity of the 12-frame 720×540 GIF to the photograph is 96.0, with the last frame 90 percent photograph and 10 percent activator. Overall 85.0. Overall 85.0/100 (faithfulness 83.6, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 85, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/aurelia_aurita_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 372994 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 a7813ce4b07c7da1e5b6848bc54a7019435498384530c87cd0855f7239fcd9ac (sha256 a7813ce4b07c7da1e5b6848bc54a7019435498384530c87cd0855f7239fcd9ac), spec_fingerprint 466a72b70c6deefab849cdaf54ef8ca2bbac24e0ab13e981975c600a6c11b298. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 466a72b70c6deefab849cdaf54ef8ca2bbac24e0ab13e981975c600a6c11b298; artifact_sha256: a7813ce4b07c7da1e5b6848bc54a7019435498384530c87cd0855f7239fcd9ac; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/aurelia_aurita_turing_wavelength_s0/aurelia_aurita_specimen.jpg=f4f54dc98dc4d9b3..., datasets/aurelia_aurita_turing_wavelength_s0/aurelia_aurita_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=dad34a0a6b9d9a54..., datasets/aurelia_aurita_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=82e768a4e917def7...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-aurelia-aurita-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a reaction-diffusion system can select a finite wavelength. | Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species kinetics implemented here. | Nakanishi, Hartenstein & Jacobs 2009: Aurelia rhopalia develop a pigment-cup ocellus. | Helm 2018: a scyphozoan medusa has eight rhopalia. | Thoma 2015 CC0 photograph of living Aurelia aurita.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.10, b=0.90, Du=1, Dv=20, gamma=1, chosen so lambda_c equals 0.0002006 m. | Spectral integration, dispersion fit (Pearson r = 0.9999), Dv sweep (r = 0.9978), equal-diffusion ablation drawn on the patterned colour scale. | Bell-body circularity after an 8 px distance threshold, and an angular lobe count on the clipped oral bell.; transfer_boundary: 201 µm is the assigned detail scale (0.0002006 m, log10 = -3.698), not a length measured on the photograph or in the cited papers.; does_not_claim: That eight rhopalia equal the bell circumference divided by 201 µm. | That the Karlsruhe photograph resolves the ocellus wavelength. | That the lobe counter recovered four gonads. It returned 1.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Addressed in pass 2. The equal-diffusion panel uses the patterned vmin/vmax. The panel is blank and the title still records std 0.0000.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Addressed in pass 2. Bell-body circularity is 0.462 after an 8 px distance threshold, against 0.328 for the pass-1 mask. It is still not a circle.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Addressed in pass 2. The lobe reference is 4 gonads. The counter returned 1. The mismatch is stored, not edited away.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Still open. A second assessor from another provider has not scored this script.', 'status': 'open'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Still open, and it should stay open. No histological measurement of a 201 µm Aurelia pigment wavelength was found. The length remains the assigned detail scale.', 'status': 'open'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.85"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent pass 2)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

